  "id": "event-memory",
  "term": "event memory",
  "definition": "Event memory is a memory representation of a consciously experienced event, including objects or actions embedded in emotional, spatial, and temporal context. In this source, it is described as an allocentric event code formed by the hippocampus and linked into sequences that make up episodic memory.",
